NAME
     fsbench - what the file system costs

SYNOPSIS
     fsbench [-d DIR] [PHASE...]

DESCRIPTION
     fsbench writes, reads, syncs and unlinks in the ways that separate
     one file system from another -- sequential and random, small files
     and big ones, metadata, a big directory, and a mixture -- and
     prints megabytes a second and operations a second for each. It is
     plain POSIX, so the same source runs on Linux for comparison
     (bench/run.py).
